## Profile APIs

### API 04 — Get My User Profile
```
GET {{base_url}}/rest/v1/users?select=id,email,first_name,last_name,role,created_at
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
```
Expected: Only the authenticated Member's profile should be visible.

### API 05 — Get My Member Profile
```
GET {{base_url}}/rest/v1/members?select=*
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
```
Expected response:
```json
[
  {
    "id": "YOUR-USER-UUID",
    "qr_token": "PRIVATE-QR-TOKEN",
    "created_at": "2026-10-30T14:10:46+00:00"
  }
]
```
Note: Do not share actual QR tokens publicly.

### API 06 — Get Member Profile by ID
```
GET {{base_url}}/rest/v1/members?id=eq.{{user_id}}&select=*
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
```
Expected: The Member can retrieve their own profile only.

### API 07 — Update Member Profile
```
PATCH {{base_url}}/rest/v1/users?id=eq.{{user_id}}
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Prefer: return=representation
Body:
{
  "first_name": "Updated",
  "last_name": "Member"
}
```
Expected: 200 OK with one updated record.

Security restrictions:
- Members must not be able to update: id, email, role, plan, created_at
- Database requirement: The Member UPDATE RLS policy and column-level permissions must be configured first.

### API 09 — Get Admin Profile
```
GET {{base_url}}/rest/v1/users?id=eq.{{admin_user_id}}&select=id,email,role
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
```

### API 10 — Admin View All Members
```
GET {{base_url}}/rest/v1/members?select=id,created_at
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
```
Expected: Admin can view Member records.
Note: Avoid selecting qr_token unless the Admin operation specifically requires it.

## Coach Application APIs

### API 26 — Submit Coach Application
```
POST {{base_url}}/rest/v1/coach_applications
Headers:
  apikey: {{anon_key}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Prefer: return=representation
Body:
{
  "user_id": "{{user_id}}",
  "experience": "3 years",
  "certification": "Personal Trainer Certification",
  "message": "I would like to apply to become a gym coach.",
  "status": "pending"
}
```
Important: The database should enforce the authenticated user's identity and pending status. Client-submitted status must not allow self-approval.

